The condition says $f(a+h) approx f(a) + A h$ for small $h$: near $a$, the function agrees with the affine map $f(a) + A h$ up to an error that is small compared with $abs(h)$. The function $epsilon(h)$ quantifies this error, and the requirement is equivalent to
$
  f(a+h) = f(a) + A h + o(abs(h)).
$
Whenever $f$ is differentiable at $a$, the constant must be $A = f'(a)$.
